  "id": "COMPOUND:26075 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Decyl propionate is implicated in the biological pathway leading to CX-1 through a series of molecular interactions involving SNU-387. The evidence suggests that Decyl propionate acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Dendocarbin K. These compounds are all linked to CX-1 as their targets, indicating a potential hierarchical relationship where Decyl propionate serves as a bridge to CX-1 via SNU-387. The consistent presence of SNU-387 as a common intermediate across different pathways supports the notion of a shared mechanism, possibly involving receptor activation or signaling pathways. The integration of these findings highlights the role of SNU-387 as a central node in the network connecting Decyl propionate to CX-1, emphasizing the importance of this intermediate in mediating the interaction between the drug and the target.",
